  "notes": "Agent re-read after the Code Health refactor, 2026-11-07, under the owner directive transcribed in verification/reviews/rulings/agent-rereview-after-refactor-2026-11-07.md. This record is NOT an owner signature: it attests the agent's substantive reading only. Read proxy.exchange_relation, the one unit whose inputs moved. This refactor moved invariant_violation and its helpers into exchange_state/invariants.rs (reached through super:: paths) and split the consequence-monotonicity test into assert_events_keep_consequence and assert_observations_keep_consequence. Other merged work changed the relation's callers: a refusal now enters its terminal through ExchangeProgress::refuse, called from the one disposition function (#1209), and may_publish consumes the ServedSuccess and returns an exchange-bound PublishPermit (#1253). The relation itself is as reviewed: transition refuses every event from a terminal state, takes Refused from every non-terminal state to RefusedBeforeDispatch or FailedAfterDispatch according to backend_may_have_executed (so a refusal cannot choose the flattering terminal), and advance latches an illegal transition in every build. All 17 previously cited tests compare equal to the old ones once indentation is ignored, and the new advance_refused_enters_the_terminal_the_relation_picks pins that a refusal from every pipeline state reaches the terminal the relation picks with no anomaly, and that a second refusal latches an anomaly and reports NotRetrySafe. The claim, scope and premises are unchanged. Evidence class as registered; V0 units are tested and probed, not machine-checked proofs. The mutation lane was not re-run by this reading; check-registries resolves every probe anchor.",
